    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nhey,\r\n\r\nI was wondering if there was a way to have multiple mappings?\r\n\r\nI have muscle memory depending on the action I'm taking, where I will use both `<C-l>` and `<CR>` depending, and I wont both to be `go_in_plus` instead of one being `go_in`\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n        mappings = {\r\n          go_in = '',\r\n          go_in_plus = { '<C-l>', '<CR>' },\r\n          go_out = '',\r\n          go_out_plus = '<C-h>',\r\n        }\r\n```",
